<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two U.S. emissaries to arrive in Pyongyang.</title>
<headline>Two U.S. emissaries to arrive in Pyongyang.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two senior U.S. emissaries left Japan for North Korea on Sunday on a three-day visit, domestic Yonhap TV said.</p>
<p>Earlier this week, Seoul's foreign ministry said former Senator Sam Nunn and former U.S. ambassador to South Korea James Laney would visit Pyongyang in a &quot;private&quot; capacity.</p>
<p>Ministry officials said the two would discuss issues relating to food aid to the hunger-stricken North and four-way peace talks involving the United States, North Korea, South Korea and China.</p>
</text>
